### ==============================================================================
### PHASE 1: AUTHENTICATION, USERS & RBAC (Shared Core API)
### Run directly inside VS Code by clicking "Send Request" above each endpoint
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. SEED DATA & DEPARTMENTS
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 List All Departments (Public / Authenticated)
# @name listDepartments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/departments
Content-Type: application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. EMPLOYEE REGISTRATION & AUTHENTICATION
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Register New Employee (Role is strictly locked to EMPLOYEE)
# @name registerEmployee
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "John",
    "lastName": "Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
    "phone": "+254711000111",
    "departmentId": "{{listDepartments.response.body.data[1].id}}"
}

### 2.2 Login as Registered Employee
# @name employeeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store Employee Tokens
@employeeToken = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}
@employeeRefreshToken = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.refreshToken}}
@employeeUserId = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.userId}}

### 2.3 Get Current Employee Profile & Hierarchy (/me)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 2.4 Verify RBAC: Employee Cannot Create Users (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Hacker",
    "lastName": "Admin",
    "email": "hacker@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "roleName": "HR_ADMIN"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. HR ADMINISTRATOR WORKFLOW
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Login as Default Seeded HR Admin
# @name hrAdminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "hr.admin@company.com",
    "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Store HR Admin Token
@adminToken = {{hrAdminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 3.2 List All Users (HR Admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.3 HR Admin Creates a Line Manager Account
# @name createManager
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Alice",
    "lastName": "Smith",
    "email": "alice.manager@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "roleName": "LINE_MANAGER",
    "jobTitle": "Engineering Lead",
    "phone": "+254722000222",
    "departmentId": "{{listDepartments.response.body.data[1].id}}"
}

### Store Manager ID
@managerId = {{createManager.response.body.data.id}}

### 3.4 HR Admin Assigns Line Manager to Employee
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/{{employeeUserId}}/manager
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}"
}

### 3.5 Re-check Employee Profile (Now reflects assigned manager in reporting_hierarchy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. TOKEN ROTATION & REVOCATION (Opaque Refresh Tokens)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Rotate Refresh Token (Generates new access token + new refresh token)
# @name refreshToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{employeeRefreshToken}}"
}

### Store Rotated Token
@newRefreshToken = {{refreshToken.response.body.data.refreshToken}}

### 4.2 Logout (Revokes Refresh Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{newRefreshToken}}"
}

### 4.3 Attempt Refresh with Revoked Token (Expect HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{newRefreshToken}}"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. RATE LIMITING (5 Failed Attempts -> 15 min Lockout)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Test 5 Failed Attempts (returns 401: "Invalid email or password")
### 6th Attempt returns 429 Too Many Requests: "Too many failed login attempts..."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 6. PHASE 2: ORGANIZATION HIERARCHY (REPORTING LINES)
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 HR Admin Assigns Manager to Employee (POST /api/identity/hierarchy/assign)
# @name assignHierarchy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}",
    "relationshipType": "DIRECT"
}

### 6.2 Caller's Current Manager (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/my-manager)
### IDOR-safe: Derives employee ID strictly from JWT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/my-manager
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 6.3 Caller's Direct Reports (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/my-subordinates)
### Called by Manager -> Returns employee list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/my-subordinates
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 6.4 HR Admin Views Any User's Direct Reports (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/{userId}/subordinates)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/{{managerId}}/subordinates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6.5 Test Validation: Reject Self-Reporting (Expect HTTP 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{employeeUserId}}"
}

### 6.6 Test Validation: Reject Assignment from Non-Admin (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}"
}

